                                                "sense_id": "304d676b-9c05-3bb0-a2fa-b678a5482ac2",
                                                "text": "scattered applause"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "750aadcc-c3f1-4923-94e1-ea3fda0bbe91",
                                                "sense_id": "304d676b-9c05-3bb0-a2fa-b678a5482ac2",
                                                "text": "And when their ſcattered armie is ſubdu’d:\nAnd you march on their ſlaughtered carkaſſes,\nShare equally the gold that bought their liues,\nAnd liue like Gentlmen in Perſea, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3858e1f3-7bd0-4025-82fc-d9548a3592bd",
                                                "sense_id": "304d676b-9c05-3bb0-a2fa-b678a5482ac2",
                                                "text": "The surroundings become bleak in the extreme as the timber line is approached and trees give place to thinly scattered birches that are little more than bushes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f79c96b2-1165-3c05-903b-0c90febbe0c3",
                                        "entry_id": "707d4109-10fd-3bd7-b7c4-752cb7a5ed4d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Seemingly randomly distributed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2fc2a7c-4302-4cfb-8ae5-9e690e93af6e",
                                                "sense_id": "f79c96b2-1165-3c05-903b-0c90febbe0c3",
                                                "text": "There were many wooden chairs for the bulk of his visitors, and two wicker armchairs with red cloth cushions for superior people. From the packing-cases had emerged some Indian clubs,[…], and all these articles[…] made a scattered and untidy decoration that Mrs. Clough assiduously dusted and greatly cherished."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c83b4a1-f37d-3828-a88d-8856d067e192",
                                        "entry_id": "707d4109-10fd-3bd7-b7c4-752cb7a5ed4d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Covering three eighths to four eighths of the sky."
                                        ],
